## Defect D1 (owner: game-developer) — game is cropped in browser viewports shorter than ~675 px
`#game` is 640 px wide with a fixed-aspect board plus HUD (~674 px total) and `body` is a centered flex box with `height:100%`, so in a shorter viewport the content overflows both ends; the top overflow is unreachable by scrolling. Measured (`results.json`, `07-*` screenshots): 1366x650 viewport → HUD top at -12 px (Score row half cut) and board bottom cut at 662 px; 1024x600 / 800x600 → top at -37 px (Score/Best hidden entirely) and bottom at 637 px. Typical laptops (1366x768 screen) have ~650 px of viewport height, so the score (R8) and the bottom row of the board (R2) are cut there. Fits at 1366x768, 1280x720, 1440x700.

Not defects / notes: pause on window blur and P pause are extras and work; best score persists in localStorage.
